error[E0450]: cannot prove `n >= 0`, the postcondition of `narrow_wrong`
  --> nat_int.ck:20:22
   |
20 | fn narrow_wrong i -> r : i~Int, r~Nat
   |                      ^ promised here
   = note: for the value returned on line 21: `i`
   = note: counterexample: i = -1
   = help: make the body establish it in every branch; facts about other functions come from their postconditions, or from a lemma brought in with `have`

error[E0450]: cannot prove that this `Nat` subtraction stays at or above zero
  --> nat_int.ck:28:5
   |
28 |     a - b
   |     ^^^^^ `-` on `Nat` needs the left side to be at least the right
   = note: counterexample: a = 0, b = 1
   = help: check it first (`if a >= b then a - b else …`), or use `Int`

error[E0262]: type mismatch: expected `List Nat`, found `List Int`
  --> nat_int.ck:32:5
   |
32 |     is
   |     ^^ this expression has type `List Int`, so its `Int` values aren't known to be `Nat`
   = note: a refinement inside a type is never gained from an existing value: that would need a proof about every element (D71)
   = help: give the value the type `List Nat` where it is built, so that each part is checked there

nat_int.ck: 3 errors, 0 warnings
